The {{nihongo|'''Okaiken national football team'''|サッカー岡井県代表|Sakkā Okaiken Daihyō}} represents [[Okaiken]] in [[wikipedia:association football|association football]] and is operated by the Okaiken Football Association (OFA), the governing body for association football in Okaiken. The current head coach is Stefan Maurice.

Known by their moniker, the '''Mighty Warriors''', the team is widely considered the undisputed powerhouse of the East Fosia Football Association (EFFA). Entering the 2026 season, Okaiken has secured its eighth consecutive qualification for the global tournament, dominating their regional group stages with an unyielding and physically aggressive style of play.

==Tactics and Playstyle==
While historically relying on agility and technical passing, the modern Okaiken team under Stefan Maurice has forged a reputation as a phenomenally tough, physically imposing, and intensely aggressive squad. Their identity is built around a relentless high-pressing system, often described as a highly disciplined ''Gegenpressing''. The moment possession is lost, the Mighty Warriors swarm their opponents in cohesive units to force critical errors deep in enemy territory.

Unlike teams that simply rely on brute force, Okaiken's aggression is instrumental and assertive. Defenders and midfielders snap into tackles and utilize their lower center of gravity to dominate one-on-one physical battles, deliberately turning matches into grueling physical tests that exhaust the opposition. This tactical evolution—combining their traditional technical superiority with an intimidating, high-intensity physical block—has propelled Okaiken back to the number one spot in the UFFA rankings for 2026.

==Recent History (2026)==
In the lead-up to the 2026 international tournament cycle, Okaiken dismantled their regional rivals with staggering efficiency, maintaining a nearly impenetrable defense. Captain Keisuke Honda and vice-captain Issei Kawada lead a locker room defined by martial discipline, ensuring that the team maintains its aggressive shape and stamina for the full 90 minutes. 

